nce"},{"tool_name":"suppliers__report_delivery_issue","type":"tool_reference"},{"tool_name":"payments__export_settlement_report","type":"tool_reference"}],"type":"tool_search_tool_search_result"},"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_01ThBsneHJ8LCH3JkokLPNBd","type":"tool_search_tool_result"},{"citations":null,"text":"I can't compare the Mother's Day and Father's Day campaigns on ROAS or cost per acquisition with the tools I have. None of them return campaign ad spend, attributed revenue, or customer acquisition data.\n\nWhat I can see:\n- **Marketing tools:** I can create and manage campaigns, promotions, discount codes, and social posts. I can also pull usage and revenue for a specific discount code, and engagement metrics for a single social post. These show parts of campaign performance, but not ROAS or CPA.\n- **Accounting and suppliers:** I can list recorded expenses by vendor, category, or date. Those could show spend, such as ad platform charges, if they're logged there. I can't tie them to a specific campaign.\n\nOptions:\n1. **Check your ad platforms directly** (Meta, Google Ads, or wherever you run these). Campaign-level spend, revenue, and conversions there will give you ROAS and CPA for each campaign.\n2. **Give me the discount codes** used for each campaign, and I'll pull redemptions and revenue from `get_discount_code_usage`. That gives a partial ROAS view if the campaigns used codes, though it leaves out ad spend.\n3. **Send me the spend and conversion figures** for each campaign, and I'll do the ROAS and CPA calculation and comparison.","type":"text"}],"diagnostics":null,"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","role":"assistant","stop_details":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"type":"message","usage":{"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":0,"inference_geo":"global","input_tokens":9499,"output_tokens":789,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":156},"server_t